# Implementation and building

This is an independent implementation of the documented command-line interface.
It uses only the Go standard library. No network access or third-party packages
are required for building.

```sh
./compile.sh
./executable -all path/to/source.go
```

The source is kept in `.src` so that generating tests in the workspace does not
accidentally include the generator's own implementation. The build script writes
`executable` in the workspace root. Build outputs are ignored by Git.

## Design

- `main.go` handles flags, validation, diagnostics, and output selection.
- `input.go` discovers files, parses Go declarations, and resolves local types.
- `model.go` represents signatures, receiver fields, and type parameters.
- `render.go` builds table-driven tests, supports template overrides, resolves
  imports, and formats the resulting source.
- `ai.go` implements the optional HTTP-based test-case generation protocol.

Source processing is syntactic: the input package does not need to compile or
have its external dependencies installed. Existing tests are retained, and only
missing tests in the corresponding test file are generated.

The implementation was developed through command-line experiments against the
provided executable, including file-writing tests and a local HTTP test server.
It does not use the provided executable at runtime.

## Regression tests

```sh
go test ./.src
```
